        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Yes, I've seen the suggested approach. But `search_mode = \"cover\"` means:\r\n\r\n- give up forward search completely, or\r\n- learn to press one more key in this situation, which as I explained is a different mental model from vanilla neovim and even other mainstream plugins, e.g. `nvim-surround`.\r\n\r\n`mini.ai` is an amazing plugin and thanks a lot for it, it's just a pity that migrating to it involves having to rewire your muscle memory.",
